                <pb facs="0614" n="534" xml:id="pg534"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">811.7442/35: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Chargé in Canada</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Riggs</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to
                        the Acting Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Ottawa</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-04-05T13:00:00-05:00">April 5, 1930—1
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 3:05 p.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>53. Department’s 38, March 29, 11 a.m. Reply to Legation’s representations of
                    March 31st received today. Department of External Affairs states in note that
                    suggested conference would be useful and that date of April 10th, 1930 in New
                    York City would be satisfactory. Delegates are stated to be Mr. C. P. Edwards,
                    Director of Radio in the Department of Marine, and Major W. A. Steel, of the
                    Department of National Defense.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Riggs</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
